{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/friction/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/friction.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Friction | Physics Mechanics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n        <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Mechanics</a>\n        </nav>\n\n        <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n            <header class=\"mb-12\">\n                <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Friction</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Understanding the force that resists relative motion between surfaces</p>\n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n                <!-- Types of Friction -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Types of Friction</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Static Friction</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Acts when object is stationary</li>\n                                <li>• Maximum value: fs ≤ μsN</li>\n                                <li>• Prevents motion initiation</li>\n                                <li>• Variable magnitude up to maximum</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Kinetic Friction</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Acts during motion</li>\n                                <li>• Constant value: fk = μkN</li>\n                                <li>• Opposes ongoing motion</li>\n                                <li>• Generally less than static friction</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Friction Coefficients -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Friction Coefficients</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Static Coefficient (μs)</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Wood on wood: 0.25-0.50</li>\n                                    <li>• Metal on metal: 0.15-0.60</li>\n                                    <li>• Rubber on concrete: 0.60-0.85</li>\n                                    <li>• Ice on ice: 0.10</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Kinetic Coefficient (μk)</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Wood on wood: 0.20</li>\n                                    <li>• Metal on metal: 0.15</li>\n                                    <li>• Rubber on concrete: 0.50</li>\n                                    <li>• Ice on ice: 0.03</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Laws and Properties -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Laws and Properties</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Basic Laws</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Proportional to normal force</li>\n                                    <li>• Independent of contact area</li>\n                                    <li>• Depends on surface properties</li>\n                                    <li>• Always parallel to surface</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Important Properties</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Direction opposes motion/tendency</li>\n                                    <li>• μs &gt; μk (usually)</li>\n                                    <li>• Temperature dependent</li>\n                                    <li>• Surface cleanliness matters</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Applications -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Applications</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Transportation</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Tire traction</li>\n                                <li>• Brake systems</li>\n                                <li>• Road design</li>\n                                <li>• Railway wheels</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Engineering</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Bearings</li>\n                                <li>• Lubricants</li>\n                                <li>• Machine design</li>\n                                <li>• Material processing</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Daily Life</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Walking</li>\n                                <li>• Writing</li>\n                                <li>• Sports</li>\n                                <li>• Household items</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Problem-Solving Examples -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Problem-Solving Examples</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Example 1: Block on Incline</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Find the minimum coefficient of static friction needed to prevent a block from sliding down a 30° incline.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-2 pl-4 text-sm text-gray-600\">\n                                    <p>Solution approach:</p>\n                                    <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-4 space-y-1\">\n                                        <li>Draw force diagram</li>\n                                        <li>Resolve forces parallel and perpendicular to incline</li>\n                                        <li>Apply equilibrium conditions</li>\n                                        <li>Solve for μs</li>\n                                    </ol>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Example 2: Pulling a Block</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Calculate the force needed to pull a 10kg block across a horizontal surface with μk = 0.2.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-2 pl-4 text-sm text-gray-600\">\n                                    <p>Key points:</p>\n                                    <ul class=\"list-disc pl-4 space-y-1\">\n                                        <li>Normal force = weight</li>\n                                        <li>Kinetic friction opposes motion</li>\n                                        <li>Use F = μkN</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n        .content-card {\n            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}